# Code: Git and project search, and the Python language server (completions, problems, go-to-definition).
# Other languages' servers (clangd, rust-analyzer, gopls, typescript-language-server…) are used when installed.
git
ripgrep
python3-pylsp
python3-pyflakes
# Format Document and formatting when saving, for Python (pylsp hands it to autopep8).
python3-autopep8
# Debugging: debugpy for Python, GDB (14 and later speak the Debug Adapter Protocol) for C, C++, Rust and Go.
python3-debugpy
gdb
# The Tests panel runs a Python project's tests with pytest; without it the panel finds none.
python3-pytest
# Game projects keep their large files (textures, models, sound) in Git LFS: without it a clone is placeholders.
git-lfs
# Code on another computer over SSH: its folder is mounted with sshfs (apps/huginn_remote.py).
sshfs
openssh-client
